# PyThani.ai — AI-Powered Saree Design & E-Commerce Platform

## Complete Technical Project Description (For External Viva Presentation)

---

## 1. Project Title

**PyThani.ai — An AI-Powered Generative Saree Design and E-Commerce Platform**

> The name "PyThani" is a portmanteau of **"Python"** (representing the language of AI & technology) and **"Paithani"** (a world-famous traditional Maharashtrian silk saree), symbolising the fusion of cutting-edge Artificial Intelligence with India's rich textile heritage.

---

## 2. Abstract

PyThani.ai is a **full-stack web application** that leverages **Generative AI (text-to-image models)** to enable users to design unique saree patterns through natural-language text prompts. The platform bridges the gap between traditional Indian textile artistry and modern AI-powered design tools by allowing customers to describe their dream saree in words (e.g., *"red Banarasi silk with gold zari work"*) and instantly receive photorealistic AI-generated saree images.

The system is built on a **three-tier architecture**:

| Tier | Technology | Purpose |
|------|-----------|---------|
| **Presentation (Frontend)** | React 19 + Vite | Customer-facing website & Admin panel |
| **Application (Backend)** | Node.js + Express 5 | RESTful API server |
| **Data (Database)** | MongoDB + Mongoose | Persistent order & user data storage |

Users can browse AI-generated designs, add them to a cart, complete a checkout with delivery details, and place orders — all backed by **Clerk authentication** for secure sign-in. A separate **Admin Panel** provides store owners with a dashboard displaying sales analytics (via Recharts) and a complete order management interface with Accept/Deny workflows.

---

## 3. Introduction & Motivation

India's handloom and textile industry is one of the largest in the world, yet saree designers and weavers often face significant challenges:

- **Long design cycles** — Creating new saree patterns traditionally takes weeks or months of manual sketching and sampling.
- **Limited creative exploration** — Artisans are constrained by their personal experience and cannot easily visualise thousands of pattern variations.
- **Digital gap** — Many small designers lack access to advanced design software (Adobe Illustrator, CAD tools).
- **No e-commerce integration** — Traditional artisans struggle to reach customers beyond local markets.

**PyThani.ai addresses all of these problems** by offering an AI-first platform where:
1. Anyone can generate production-quality saree designs using simple English text prompts.
2. The AI engine (powered by **FLUX-Schnell** via Puter.js) generates 4 unique photorealistic saree images per query in under 30 seconds.
3. Users can immediately add designs to cart and place orders with full checkout flow.
4. Admins can manage the order pipeline from a dedicated dashboard.

