## 8. Module-Wise Detailed Description

### 8.1 Module 1: Customer-Facing Website (`saree-website/`)

This is the primary user-facing application — a modern, animated, single-page React app.

#### 8.1.1 Entry Point & Providers (`main.jsx`)

```
ReactDOM.createRoot → <ClerkProvider> → <BrowserRouter> → <App />
```

- **ClerkProvider** wraps the entire app, injecting authentication context via the publishable key stored in `.env` (`VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`).
- **BrowserRouter** enables client-side routing with the History API.
- The Clerk publishable key is loaded from environment variables using `import.meta.env` (Vite's built-in env handling).

#### 8.1.2 Root Component (`App.jsx`) — State Management & Business Logic

The `App` component acts as the **central state manager** for the entire application. It manages:

| State Variable | Type | Purpose |
|---------------|------|---------|
| `cartItems` | `Array<Object>` | Local shopping cart (stored in React state, not DB) |
| `isCartOpen` | `Boolean` | Controls the CartDrawer slide-in visibility |

**Key Functions:**

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `handleAddToCart(item)` | Generates a temporary `_id` using `Date.now()`, copies `imageUrl` and `price`, appends to `cartItems` array, and opens the cart drawer |
| `handleRemoveFromCart(itemId)` | Filters out the item with matching `_id` from `cartItems` |
| `handlePlaceOrder(formData)` | Makes a `POST /api/orders` request to the backend with `userId` (from Clerk), `cartItems`, and `userDetails` (address form). On success, clears the cart |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Design Decision**: The cart is managed entirely in **client-side React state** (not persisted to the database). The database is only contacted when the user **places a final order**. This reduces unnecessary API calls and keeps the experience fast.

#### 8.1.3 SearchPage Component (`pages/SearchPage.jsx`) — The Core AI Page

This is the **most important component** — the main page users interact with. It contains **12 distinct UI sections**, all on a single scrollable page:

| # | Section | Description |
|---|---------|-------------|
| 1 | **Hero Section** | Full-width banner with heading "Design Your Dream Saree with AI", subtitle, CTA buttons, and a 4-image gallery |
| 2 | **Prompt Search Bar** | Text input with search icon + "Generate" button. Supports `Enter` key submission |
| 3 | **Quick Design Ideas** | 16 pre-written prompt chips (e.g., "🔴 Red Banarasi Silk"). Clicking auto-fills the search bar and triggers generation |
| 4 | **Results Grid** | Masonry-style grid displaying AI-generated `DesignCard` components as they arrive (progressive loading) |
| 5 | **"Inspired by Tradition"** | Split-layout section with descriptive text + side gallery images |
| 6 | **Empowering Weavers** | Feature list (AI Pattern Generation, Virtual Draping, Color Palette) with stacked image gallery |
| 7 | **Data Stats** | KPI section showing "2B+ Designs Generated", "200K+ Artisans", "10M+ Motifs" |
| 8 | **AI Toolkit** | 3-card grid showcasing AI Motif Generator, Virtual Saree Draper, AI Colorway Creator |
| 9 | **Gallery of Innovation** | 6-image masonry gallery of saree designs |
| 10 | **Testimonial** | Customer quote with avatar, pagination dots |
| 11 | **About Us** | PyThani brand story with image gallery |
| 12 | **Final CTA** | "Start Designing Your Saree Today" call-to-action |

**AI Image Generation Pipeline:**

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant SearchPage
    participant PuterJS as Puter.js SDK (Browser)
    participant FLUX as FLUX-Schnell Model (Cloud)

    User->>SearchPage: Types "red Banarasi silk with gold zari"
    User->>SearchPage: Clicks "Generate"
    SearchPage->>SearchPage: Enhances prompt with prefix:<br/>"photorealistic full-body portrait of<br/>a beautiful Indian woman model<br/>wearing an elegant draped Saree,<br/>studio lighting, fashion photography, {user_prompt}"

    loop 4 iterations (i = 0 to 3)
        SearchPage->>PuterJS: puter.ai.txt2img(enhancedPrompt, {model: 'flux-schnell'})
        PuterJS->>FLUX: API Request (Cloud Inference)
        FLUX-->>PuterJS: Generated Image (Base64 Data URL)
        PuterJS-->>SearchPage: <img> element with .src = base64
        SearchPage->>SearchPage: setResults(prev => [...prev, {id, imageUrl: imgEl.src, price: random(2000-6000)}])
        Note over SearchPage: Image appears immediately (progressive rendering)
        SearchPage->>SearchPage: Wait 1500ms (rate-limit delay)
    end
```

> [!NOTE]
> **Prompt Engineering**: The user's raw input is automatically enhanced with a professional photography prefix to ensure the AI generates high-quality, contextually appropriate saree images rather than abstract patterns.

**Scroll Animations:**
The page uses `react-intersection-observer` with 11 separate `useInView()` hooks to trigger CSS `fade-in-section` → `is-visible` class toggling as each section enters the viewport.

#### 8.1.4 DesignCard Component (`components/DesignCard.jsx`)

Each AI-generated result is rendered as a `DesignCard`:
- Displays the saree image with a price badge overlay (e.g., "Rs. 3,450")
- On hover: shows a dark overlay with two buttons — **"View Details"** and **"Add to Cart"**
