  - Weave pattern (Jacquard, Brocade, Jamdani, etc.)
  - Color, Length, Weight, Border style, Pallu design
  - Occasion suitability, Blouse piece inclusion, Wash care
  - Star rating (3.8–5.0) and review count
  - Discounted price with MRP and "40% OFF" badge
- **CTA**: "Add to Cart" button (or "Sign In & Add to Cart" for unauthenticated users)

> [!NOTE]
> The specifications are **randomly generated** from curated pools of realistic saree attributes using `generateSpecs()`. This simulates a real e-commerce product detail page.

#### 8.1.6 CartDrawer Component (`components/CartDrawer.jsx`)

A **slide-in drawer** from the right side with three views:

| View | Trigger | Content |
|------|---------|---------|
| **Cart Items List** | Default when cart has items | Thumbnail, title "AI Generated Design #N", price, Remove button |
| **Checkout Form** | User clicks "Proceed to Checkout" | Form with: First Name, Last Name, Mobile (10-digit validation), Delivery Address, Payment Method (COD / UPI) |
| **Success Message** | After order is placed | "Thank You, {firstName}! Your order has been placed successfully. We will contact you at {mobile} shortly." (auto-closes after 3 seconds) |

#### 8.1.7 Navbar Component (`components/Navbar.jsx`)

- **Left**: PyThani logo image (linked to home)
- **Center**: Navigation links — Home, About (anchor `#about`), Features (anchor `#features`)
- **Right**: Cart icon with badge count + Auth button
  - Signed in: Clerk `<UserButton>` (avatar, profile, sign-out)
  - Not signed in: Clerk `<SignInButton>` (opens modal)

#### 8.1.8 Vite Proxy Configuration (`vite.config.js`)

A **reverse proxy** is configured to handle Freepik API requests:
```
/api/* → https://api.freepik.com/*
```
- Injects the `x-freepik-api-key` header automatically
- This avoids CORS issues and keeps the API key hidden from the browser's network tab

