### 8.2 Module 2: Backend Server (`server/`)

A **Node.js + Express 5** REST API server providing 5 endpoints.

#### 8.2.1 Server Configuration (`index.js`)

| Configuration | Value | Purpose |
|--------------|-------|---------|
| Port | 5001 | Avoids conflict with frontend dev servers (5173/5174) |
| JSON limit | 50 MB | Supports large Base64-encoded AI-generated images in order payloads |
| URL-encoded limit | 50 MB | Same as above |
| CORS | Open (all origins) | Allows requests from both frontend apps |
| MongoDB URI | `mongodb://localhost:27017/pythaniDB` | Local development database |

#### 8.2.2 API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose | Request Body | Response |
|--------|----------|---------|-------------|----------|
| `GET` | `/` | Health check | — | `"Hello from the PyThani Server!"` |
| `POST` | `/api/orders` | Create new order | `{ userId, items: [{imageUrl}], userDetails: {firstName, lastName, mobile, address, paymentMethod} }` | `201 Created` + saved order JSON |
| `GET` | `/api/admin/orders` | Fetch all orders (newest first) | — | Array of order objects |
| `GET` | `/api/admin/stats` | Fetch aggregated statistics | — | `{ totalOrders, totalSales, processingOrders, deliveredOrders }` |
| `PATCH` | `/api/admin/orders/:id/status` | Update order status | `{ status: "Accepted" \| "Cancelled" }` | Updated order object |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Data Sanitization**: In the `POST /api/orders` endpoint, the server creates a `cleanedItems` array that **strips out the `_id`** sent by the frontend, keeping only the `imageUrl`. This prevents MongoDB `CastError` exceptions caused by the temporary `Date.now()` IDs generated client-side.

#### 8.2.3 Database Models (Mongoose Schemas)

**Order Model (`models/Order.js`)**:
```
Order {
  userId:       String (required)       — Clerk user ID
  items:        [{imageUrl: String}]    — Array of saree image URLs
  userDetails:  {                       — Embedded document
    firstName:     String
    lastName:      String
    mobile:        String
    address:       String
    paymentMethod: String
  }
  createdAt:    Date (default: now)     — Timestamp
}
```

**CartItem Model (`models/CartItem.js`)**:
```
CartItem {
  imageUrl:  String (required)  — Saree image URL
  userId:    String (required)  — Clerk user ID
  createdAt: Date (default: now)
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> The `CartItem` model exists as a **legacy schema** from an earlier design where the cart was server-side. In the current architecture, the cart is fully client-side (React state), so this model is not actively used — but the schema remains for potential future use (e.g., persistent carts across sessions).

